---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const post = {
 title: 'ANSI/ISEA 107 Hi-Vis Guide for Branded Workwear',
 description:
 'A practical guide to employer selection, garment labels, manufacturer documents, and decoration review for ANSI/ISEA 107 high-visibility apparel.',
 category: 'ANSI/ISEA 107',
 readTime: '9 min read',
 date: 'May 9, 2026',
 isoDate: '2026-05-09',
 image: '/images/generated/service-screen-printing.jpg',
 slug: 'ansi-107-hi-vis-guide',
}

const faqs = [
 { q: 'What is ANSI/ISEA 107?', a: 'ANSI/ISEA 107 is a consensus standard for high-visibility safety apparel and accessories. Use the current standard, exact garment label, employer hazard assessment, and project requirements.' },
 { q: 'Does every construction worker need the same hi-vis class?', a: 'No. The employer selects the garment type and performance class from the actual hazards and applicable project rules. Do not use one trade, speed, or job title as a universal shortcut.' },
 { q: 'Can Bighorn certify an ANSI 107 garment?', a: 'No. The garment manufacturer provides the classification and product documentation. Bighorn can quote selected products and coordinate a decoration proposal for employer review.' },
 { q: 'Can a logo be added to a hi-vis garment?', a: 'Decoration may affect required background or reflective material. Review the exact garment and scaled proof with the employer and manufacturer before production.' },
 { q: 'Is there one universal logo size limit?', a: 'No. Available area varies by garment, class, size, configuration, and current standard. Use the manufacturer decoration guide or written approval for the exact product.' },
]

const schema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@graph': [
  {
   '@type': 'Article', headline: post.title, description: post.description,
   image: `https://bighornthreads.com${post.image}`, datePublished: post.isoDate,
   dateModified: '2026-08-21',
   author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' },
   publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/images/logos/bighorn-logo-color.png' } },
   mainEntityOfPage: `https://bighornthreads.com/safety-compliance/${post.slug}/`,
  },
  {
   '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
   itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Safety and Compliance', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/safety-compliance/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: post.title, item: `https://bighornthreads.com/safety-compliance/${post.slug}/` },
   ],
  },
  { '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: faq.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.a } })) },
 ],
}
---

<BaseLayout title={post.title} description={post.description} canonical={`https://bighornthreads.com/safety-compliance/${post.slug}/`} ogImage={post.image} type="article" publishedDate={post.isoDate}>
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
 <article class="bg-concrete">
  <header class="border-b border-hairline bg-navy-950 text-white">
   <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-20 pb-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24 lg:px-8">
    <nav class="mb-6 font-mono text-xs text-navy-200" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
     <a href="/" class="hover:text-gold-400">Home</a><span class="px-2">/</span><a href="/safety-compliance/" class="hover:text-gold-400">Safety &amp; Compliance</a>
    </nav>
    <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-400">{post.category}</span>
    <h1 class="mb-6 font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">{post.title}</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-xl leading-relaxed text-navy-100">How to select and decorate high-visibility apparel without replacing the employer's hazard assessment.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 border-t border-navy-700 pt-6 font-mono text-sm text-navy-200">
     <span class="text-gold-400">Bighorn Threads Team</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span>{post.readTime}</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><time datetime={post.isoDate}>{post.date}</time>
    </div>
   </div>
  </header>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <img src={post.image} alt="High-visibility garments prepared for employer and manufacturer review" width="1200" height="675" loading="eager" class="w-full border border-hairline object-cover" />
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <aside class="mb-10 border border-hairline bg-panel p-7">
    <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-600">Quick Answer</p>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal sm:text-xl">Start with the employer's hazard assessment and project rules. Then verify the exact garment label and current manufacturer documents. Review any decoration as part of the complete finished garment.</p>
   </aside>

   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">This guide helps buyers ask better questions. It does not select PPE or certify compliance. The employer and safety lead remain responsible for product selection and use.</p>

   <h2 id="standard" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">What ANSI/ISEA 107 Covers</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal"><a href="https://safetyequipment.org/standards/ansi-isea-107/" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="text-gold-700 underline hover:text-gold-600">ANSI/ISEA 107</a> addresses high-visibility safety apparel and accessories. The current standard defines garment types, performance classes, background material, reflective material, labeling, and other criteria.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Requirements can also come from an employer, project owner, agency, contract, or site plan. Confirm which documents govern the actual work.</p>

   <h2 id="selection" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">How to Select the Garment</h2>
   <ol class="mb-8 ml-6 list-decimal space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
    <li><strong>Assess the work.</strong> Document traffic, equipment, lighting, weather, task, and site conditions.</li>
    <li><strong>Identify governing requirements.</strong> Gather employer, project, agency, and contract documents.</li>
    <li><strong>Select the exact product.</strong> Record the manufacturer, model, type, class, size range, and color.</li>
    <li><strong>Verify the label.</strong> Match the product to current manufacturer documentation.</li>
    <li><strong>Approve the complete garment.</strong> Include all decoration and accessories in the review.</li>
   </ol>

   <h2 id="class" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Type and Performance Class Are Job Specific</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Do not assign a class from one speed number, trade label, or rule of thumb. The employer must connect the selected product to the actual hazard assessment and applicable requirements.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Garment designs differ. Vests, shirts, jackets, pants, and supplemental items can provide different configurations. Use the exact label and current product sheet.</p>

   <h2 id="decoration" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Review Decoration Before Production</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">A logo can cover background or reflective material. Embroidery adds thread, backing, and needle penetrations. Printing adds ink and a curing process.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Create a scaled proof for the exact garment and size range. Include every logo, name, badge, and identifier. Ask the garment manufacturer to approve the proposed materials, method, size, and placement in writing.</p>
   <ul class="mb-8 ml-6 list-disc space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
    <li>Keep required reflective material and product labels unobstructed.</li>
    <li>Do not assume one placement works across every size or style.</li>
    <li>Review substitutions as new products, not automatic equivalents.</li>
    <li>Keep approvals and final proofs with the order record.</li>
   </ul>

   <h2 id="quote" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">What to Put in the Quote</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">A useful proposal identifies the exact garment, quantities, sizes, color, available documentation, decoration plan, pricing, and expected timing. It should also state any substitutions, freight, and approval dependencies.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Bighorn coordinates selected products through production partners. Availability and terms require written confirmation.</p>

   <section class="mt-12 border border-hairline bg-panel p-8">
    <h2 class="mb-3 font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-charcoal">Need a hi-vis apparel proposal?</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-ash">Send the employer requirements, project documents, crew sizes, and logo. We will build a product and decoration proposal for review.</p>
    <a href="/get-a-quote/" class="btn-primary text-base">Get a Quote</a>
   </section>

   <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="mb-6 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5">
     {faqs.map((faq) => (
      <div class="border border-hairline bg-paper p-6">
       <h3 class="mb-2 font-heading text-xl font-bold text-charcoal">{faq.q}</h3>
       <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ash">{faq.a}</p>
      </div>
     ))}
    </div>
   </section>
  </div>
 </article>
</BaseLayout>
